# Example secrets for running GitHub Actions locally with nektos/act.
# Copy this file to `.github/act.secrets` and replace placeholder values as needed.
# Format: KEY=VALUE (one per line)

# Mandatory for many workflows that need auth to GitHub API or GHCR.
# For local read-only runs you can set a dummy string; for pushes/comments use a PAT.
GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your_token_or_dummy

# Optional: if you use a private GHCR namespace locally
# GHCR_USER=your-gh-username
# GHCR_TOKEN=ghp_your_ghcr_pat

# Notes:
# - Workflows compose the full image as `${CI_IMAGE_REPO}:${CI_IMAGE_TAG}`
#   where CI_IMAGE_REPO defaults to `ghcr.io/costscope/ci-base`.
# - If you prefer digest pin, set CI_IMAGE_TAG to the digest and ensure workflows
#   handle it accordingly (or set CI_IMAGE_REF directly in your environment).## Example secrets file for `act` (GitHub Actions local runner)
# Copy to .github/act.secrets and populate values as needed. This example is safe to commit.

GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_examplePERSONALACCESSTOKEN
GH_PAT_RELEASE=
COSIGN_EXPERIMENTAL=1
